# APC slash commands

When the user message contains **`/apc-`** or deprecated **`/dream`**, **`/plan`**, **`/design`**, **`/impl`**, **`/ship`**, **`/status`**, **`/resume`** (plugin context):

1. Load **`.agents/skills/audio-plugin-coder/SKILL.md`** (command router).
2. Load the matching **`.agents/workflows/apc-<phase>.md`** file.
3. Execute the matching **`.agents/skills/<phase>/SKILL.md`** (or `dream`, `plan`, `impl`, …).
4. Read/update **`plugins/<PluginName>/status.json`** using `scripts/lib/apc-state.sh` patterns.
5. **Stop after one phase** unless user said `/apc-new` or asked to continue.

| Command | Phase skill |
|---------|-------------|
| `/apc-setup` | `apc-setup` |
| `/apc-dream` | `dream` |
| `/apc-plan` | `plan` |
| `/apc-design` | `design` |
| `/apc-impl` | `impl` |
| `/apc-test` | `test` |
| `/apc-debug` | `debug` |
| `/apc-ship` | `ship` |
| `/apc-status` | workflows only |
| `/apc-resume` | workflows only |

**Part 2 walkthrough:** dream phase uses `plugins/<Name>/references/` + `.ideas/creative-brief.md` + `parameter-spec.md`.

**Build:** `bash bin/apc build <Name>` — not raw cmake unless debugging.
